WEBVTT

00:00:02.252 --> 00:00:04.015
Most of the people
on this colony

00:00:04.054 --> 00:00:05.817
will remember
my grandmother as a healer

00:00:05.856 --> 00:00:08.154
but her abilities
went beyond that.

00:00:08.191 --> 00:00:11.354
She didn't just relieve pain
and fight illness.

00:00:11.395 --> 00:00:15.058
She knew that well-being is
more than just a healthy body.

00:00:15.098 --> 00:00:16.725
Her remedies

00:00:16.767 --> 00:00:20.396
often included words of advice
as well as medicinal teas

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:23.736
and often they were
just as bitter-tasting.

00:00:23.774 --> 00:00:27.471
I will miss Felisa Howard
very much...

00:00:27.511 --> 00:00:29.911
her healing, her advice

00:00:30.013 --> 00:00:33.346
and most of all the inspiration

00:00:33.383 --> 00:00:37.717
she has provided me
throughout the years.

00:00:37.754 --> 00:00:39.949
Rest in peace, Nana.

00:00:46.129 --> 00:00:49.326
And so now we commit her body
to the ground...

00:00:49.366 --> 00:00:54.531
earth to earth,
ashes to ashes, dust to dust...

00:00:54.571 --> 00:00:56.801
in sure and certain hope

00:00:56.840 --> 00:01:01.038
that her memory will be
kept alive within us all.

00:01:01.078 --> 00:01:02.909
Amen.

00:02:04.374 --> 00:02:08.777
Space, the final frontier.

00:02:08.811 --> 00:02:12.645
These are the voyages
of the Starship Enterprise.

00:02:12.682 --> 00:02:14.650
Its continuing mission...

00:02:14.684 --> 00:02:18.620
to explore strange new worlds

00:02:18.655 --> 00:02:23.092
to seek out new life
and new civilizations

00:02:23.126 --> 00:02:28.063
to boldly go
where no one has gone before.

00:03:28.324 --> 00:03:30.121
That was beautiful.

00:03:30.159 --> 00:03:32.093
Oh, thank you.

00:03:32.128 --> 00:03:36.326
Deanna, did you notice
a strange man at the service?

00:03:36.365 --> 00:03:39.664
He was in his mid-30s,
with longish hair.

00:03:39.702 --> 00:03:41.329
No.

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:46.433
He threw a flower
on Nana's grave... a camellia.

00:03:46.475 --> 00:03:48.238
It was her favorite flower.

00:03:48.277 --> 00:03:49.335
She used to keep them

00:03:49.378 --> 00:03:50.402
all over the house.

00:03:50.446 --> 00:03:52.880
Maybe he was a friend
or one of her patients.

00:03:52.915 --> 00:03:55.850
It was a very personal gesture

00:03:55.885 --> 00:03:58.683
and he gave me
a remarkable look.

00:03:58.721 --> 00:04:02.020
Well... I guess I should be
going back to the house.

00:04:02.057 --> 00:04:04.321
There are some things
I need to do.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.555
It's only
a few minutes from here.

00:04:06.595 --> 00:04:08.722
Would you mind coming along?

00:04:08.764 --> 00:04:10.231
I'd love to.

00:04:10.266 --> 00:04:11.756
Thanks.

00:04:20.075 --> 00:04:22.043
How long do you plan on staying?

00:04:22.077 --> 00:04:23.772
A few more hours.
Why?

00:04:23.813 --> 00:04:25.838
Well, as you know, Caldos

00:04:25.881 --> 00:04:28.111
is one of the first
terraforming projects

00:04:28.150 --> 00:04:29.617
of the Federation.

00:04:29.652 --> 00:04:32.052
Our weather controls
and fusion systems

00:04:32.087 --> 00:04:33.884
are nearly a century old.

00:04:33.989 --> 00:04:36.583
I wouldn't mind having
a starship engineer

00:04:36.625 --> 00:04:38.115
take a look at them.

00:04:38.160 --> 00:04:40.287
Perhaps give us a few upgrades.

00:04:40.329 --> 00:04:42.854
Maybe in exchange
for a tour of the colony

00:04:42.898 --> 00:04:45.389
and a home-cooked meal?

00:04:45.434 --> 00:04:48.164
Well, we are due
at Starbase 621 tomorrow morning

00:04:48.204 --> 00:04:50.365
but we could delay
for a few days.

00:04:50.406 --> 00:04:52.806
Yes, I'm sure we could
find the time.

00:04:52.842 --> 00:04:53.809
Excellent.

00:04:53.843 --> 00:04:55.140
I would enjoy that tour.

00:04:55.177 --> 00:04:58.237
Caldos colony is a most
impressive accomplishment.

00:04:58.280 --> 00:05:00.908
I actually feel as if I'm
in the Scottish Highlands.

00:05:00.950 --> 00:05:02.975
Well, that was the intent.

00:05:03.018 --> 00:05:05.748
The cornerstone
of every building in town

00:05:05.788 --> 00:05:09.417
was brought from Edinburgh,
Glasgow, Aberdeen.

00:05:09.458 --> 00:05:12.052
The founders wanted
everyone to feel

00:05:12.094 --> 00:05:15.359
that they had a piece
of the real thing here.

00:05:15.397 --> 00:05:18.366
They didn't want
to just imitate Scotland...

00:05:18.400 --> 00:05:20.595
they wanted to re-create it.

00:05:20.636 --> 00:05:23.196
Tell me, Governor, I'm curious.

00:05:23.239 --> 00:05:25.799
You're obviously
not Scot yourself.

00:05:25.841 --> 00:05:28.435
What was it
that drew you here?

00:05:28.477 --> 00:05:33.278
Oh, something
about the culture, the heritage.

00:05:33.315 --> 00:05:35.283
When I was a boy

00:05:35.317 --> 00:05:39.720
my family visited Glamis Castle
in Scotland

00:05:39.755 --> 00:05:43.885
and as I looked out
across the Highlands

00:05:43.926 --> 00:05:47.123
I felt as if I had come home.

00:06:15.224 --> 00:06:19.684
Your grandmother
had remarkable green eyes.

00:06:19.728 --> 00:06:22.561
Every Howard woman
has had green eyes

00:06:22.598 --> 00:06:25.089
except for my mother and me.

00:06:25.134 --> 00:06:27.864
How well
do you remember your mother?

00:06:27.970 --> 00:06:29.870
Very well.

00:06:29.972 --> 00:06:32.668
I loved her very much.

00:06:32.708 --> 00:06:38.203
I can remember...

00:06:38.247 --> 00:06:40.875
her face smiling down at me

00:06:40.916 --> 00:06:42.076
and I can remember

00:06:42.117 --> 00:06:44.608
the sound of her voice
and her scent

00:06:44.653 --> 00:06:48.214
but, mostly, I remember Nana

00:06:48.257 --> 00:06:52.421
who raised me
after my mother died.

00:06:52.461 --> 00:06:53.894
That's beautiful.

00:06:53.963 --> 00:06:55.624
It's a family heirloom.

00:06:55.664 --> 00:06:59.065
It's been in the Howard clan
for generations.

00:06:59.101 --> 00:07:02.593
It's supposed to symbolize
the "enduring Howard spirit

00:07:02.638 --> 00:07:04.105
"wherever they may go-

00:07:04.139 --> 00:07:07.597
the shining light to guide them
through their fortune."

00:07:07.643 --> 00:07:09.338
Nana always kept it lit.

00:07:09.378 --> 00:07:12.609
I remember sitting here,
listening to ghost stories

00:07:12.648 --> 00:07:14.616
with only the candle burning.

00:07:14.650 --> 00:07:17.414
You should take it with you.

00:07:17.453 --> 00:07:19.080
I think I will.

00:07:19.121 --> 00:07:22.249
I'm going to head back
to the ship.

00:07:22.291 --> 00:07:24.156
You don't have to leave.

00:07:24.193 --> 00:07:26.718
I just thought
you'd like some time alone.

00:07:26.762 --> 00:07:28.195
I'll see you later.

00:07:28.230 --> 00:07:29.891
Thanks.

00:08:51.980 --> 00:08:54.312
Who's there?

00:08:54.349 --> 00:08:55.839
What the hell are you doing?

00:08:55.884 --> 00:08:57.044
Get out of my house.

00:08:57.086 --> 00:08:58.781
I wouldn't be so high
and mighty with me

00:08:58.821 --> 00:08:59.810
Beverly Howard Crusher.

00:08:59.855 --> 00:09:01.720
I spent more time here
in the past five years

00:09:01.757 --> 00:09:03.315
than you have in the past 20.

00:09:03.358 --> 00:09:05.451
How do you know who I am?

00:09:05.494 --> 00:09:06.461
I'm Ned Quint.

00:09:06.495 --> 00:09:07.757
I took care
of your grandmother's house

00:09:07.796 --> 00:09:08.763
and her affairs.

00:09:08.797 --> 00:09:10.389
Nana never mentioned you.

00:09:10.432 --> 00:09:12.832
Oh, there's lots of things
she didna talk about.

00:09:12.935 --> 00:09:14.664
Let me get rid of that candle.

00:09:14.703 --> 00:09:15.829
Why?

00:09:15.904 --> 00:09:17.769
That candle has brought
nothing but misery

00:09:17.806 --> 00:09:19.603
and bad luck
to your grandmother.

00:09:19.641 --> 00:09:20.699
Look, Mr. Quint, I don't know

00:09:20.742 --> 00:09:22.471
what your relationship was
with my grandmother

00:09:22.511 --> 00:09:24.342
but this is my house now
and these are my things.

00:09:24.379 --> 00:09:27.837
That candle has been a curse
on your family for generations.

00:09:27.950 --> 00:09:29.577
Now, if you have a lick of sense

00:09:29.618 --> 00:09:31.848
you'll listen to me
right now do away with it.

00:09:31.887 --> 00:09:33.081
Now give it to me.

00:09:33.122 --> 00:09:35.420
This is a family heirloom
and I intend to keep it!

00:09:35.457 --> 00:09:37.357
Now would you please
get out of my house.

00:09:37.392 --> 00:09:38.689
Now!

00:09:38.727 --> 00:09:42.060
Howard women... always
the same stubborn fools.

00:09:43.465 --> 00:09:45.092
I wash my hands of it now.

00:09:45.134 --> 00:09:47.625
You stay on in this house

00:09:47.669 --> 00:09:49.864
and you keep that damned candle.

00:09:49.972 --> 00:09:52.873
I'll not be responsible
for what happens.

00:09:52.908 --> 00:09:54.239
Get out!

00:10:02.217 --> 00:10:04.879
The colony's aqueduct system
is functioning normally

00:10:04.986 --> 00:10:06.715
as are the communication relays.

00:10:06.754 --> 00:10:09.518
We've been having a few tremors
the last couple of months.

00:10:09.557 --> 00:10:11.388
Could you check
the seismic stabilizers?

00:10:11.426 --> 00:10:12.393
Certainly.

00:10:12.427 --> 00:10:13.860
You can't imagine what it's like

00:10:13.895 --> 00:10:16.455
trying to enjoy afternoon tea
while the earth is shaking.

00:10:16.497 --> 00:10:19.159
Governor, did you know
you had a power fluctuation

00:10:19.200 --> 00:10:20.861
in your weather control system?

00:10:20.902 --> 00:10:23.564
No, our weather control's
been working perfectly

00:10:23.605 --> 00:10:24.833
for the last 22 years.

00:10:24.872 --> 00:10:26.635
I can't isolate the exact source

00:10:26.674 --> 00:10:29.074
but the fluctuation
seems to be originating

00:10:29.110 --> 00:10:31.476
from one of the substations
that regulates

00:10:31.512 --> 00:10:33.503
atmospheric humidity
for the colony.

00:10:33.548 --> 00:10:35.209
Is this going to be a problem?

00:10:35.250 --> 00:10:37.775
No, not yet,
but power distribution patterns

00:10:37.819 --> 00:10:39.309
are already off by five percent.

00:10:39.354 --> 00:10:42.448
I suggest we analyze
the planet's weather patterns

00:10:42.490 --> 00:10:44.583
to see
if they have been affected.

00:10:44.626 --> 00:10:46.856
I am reading
unusually high humidity

00:10:46.894 --> 00:10:49.385
across the entire
southern desert region

00:10:49.430 --> 00:10:50.863
and there is increasing
cloud activity

00:10:50.898 --> 00:10:52.160
above the northern
coastal area...

00:10:52.200 --> 00:10:54.668
possibly the formation
of a storm system.

00:10:54.702 --> 00:10:56.795
A storm?
It's the middle of summer.

00:10:56.838 --> 00:10:59.068
We don't have rain
at this time of year.

00:10:59.107 --> 00:11:00.904
Data, let's see
if we can correct this.

00:11:00.942 --> 00:11:03.376
I'll check out the colony's
climatic flow array.

00:11:03.411 --> 00:11:07.142
I will run a diagnostic
on the thermal regulators.

00:11:07.181 --> 00:11:08.614
Don't worry, Governor.

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:09.878
We'll keep you dry.

00:11:09.917 --> 00:11:11.282
I certainly hope so.

00:11:11.319 --> 00:11:14.777
There's a caber toss scheduled
for tomorrow afternoon.

00:11:14.822 --> 00:11:18.280
I'd hate to see it spoiled
by an unexpected downpour.

00:11:20.094 --> 00:11:22.221
You wouldn't believe
what I've been reading about

00:11:22.263 --> 00:11:23.992
in my grandmother's journals.

00:11:24.032 --> 00:11:25.897
You know she had a lover.

00:11:26.000 --> 00:11:27.262
Do you believe that?

00:11:27.302 --> 00:11:28.769
Nana was 100 years old.

00:11:28.803 --> 00:11:31.567
Mmm. It would seem
that the Howard women

00:11:31.606 --> 00:11:34.040
have exceptionally
vigorous libidos.

00:11:34.075 --> 00:11:35.702
I certainly hope so.

00:11:35.743 --> 00:11:39.110
After all, I hope I can find
a handsome young man in his 30s

00:11:39.147 --> 00:11:40.910
when I've passed
the century mark.

00:11:40.948 --> 00:11:42.108
Thirties?

00:11:42.150 --> 00:11:44.414
Yes. According to these journals

00:11:44.452 --> 00:11:47.080
his name is Ronin
and he's 34 years old.

00:11:47.121 --> 00:11:51.319
They met just after
my great-grandmother's death

00:11:51.359 --> 00:11:54.021
and I think I saw him
at the funeral.

00:11:54.062 --> 00:11:57.623
A handsome young man tossed
a camellia onto her grave

00:11:57.665 --> 00:12:00.156
but the strange thing is

00:12:00.201 --> 00:12:03.796
she never mentioned him
in her letters, never once

00:12:03.838 --> 00:12:04.998
and yet it appears

00:12:05.039 --> 00:12:07.735
they spent almost all
their time together.

00:12:07.775 --> 00:12:10.767
It's as if she led
an entire life

00:12:10.812 --> 00:12:12.609
that I knew nothing about.

00:12:12.647 --> 00:12:15.707
Well, it looks as if we're going
to be on Caldos

00:12:15.750 --> 00:12:17.877
for a few days more.

00:12:17.919 --> 00:12:20.046
This will be a good opportunity

00:12:20.088 --> 00:12:22.454
for you to get your
grandmother's affairs in order.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:24.014
Thank you.

00:12:28.996 --> 00:12:30.987
Thirties?

00:13:17.979 --> 00:13:19.640
Beverly...

00:13:28.956 --> 00:13:31.117
You dreamt you were in bed
with someone?

00:13:31.159 --> 00:13:32.626
Not exactly.

00:13:32.660 --> 00:13:33.786
I was in bed

00:13:33.828 --> 00:13:36.888
but there wasn't another person
in my dream.

00:13:36.964 --> 00:13:40.422
It was more like a presence.

00:13:40.468 --> 00:13:42.026
You said you felt a touch.

00:13:42.069 --> 00:13:43.536
A pair of hands.

00:13:43.571 --> 00:13:46.506
They were moving across my skin.

00:13:46.541 --> 00:13:48.600
Like a caress?

00:13:48.643 --> 00:13:51.908
Yes, and there was a voice,
a man.

00:13:51.946 --> 00:13:54.005
He whispered my name.

00:13:54.048 --> 00:13:56.346
It was as if I knew him

00:13:56.384 --> 00:13:58.750
or more like he knew me.

00:13:58.786 --> 00:14:01.550
He knew exactly
how I liked to be touched.

00:14:01.589 --> 00:14:05.150
It was the most physical dream
I've ever had.

00:14:07.161 --> 00:14:09.959
The sensations were very real

00:14:09.997 --> 00:14:13.865
and extremely arousing.

00:14:13.968 --> 00:14:16.528
Frankly, I'm envious.

00:14:16.571 --> 00:14:20.029
I did fall asleep reading
a particularly erotic chapter

00:14:20.074 --> 00:14:21.871
in my grandmother's journal.

00:14:21.909 --> 00:14:24.173
She wrote
very detailed descriptions

00:14:24.212 --> 00:14:26.180
of her experiences with Ronin.

00:14:26.214 --> 00:14:29.377
Well, that's bound
to cause a dream or two.

00:14:29.417 --> 00:14:33.285
So, shall we start going
over the personnel reports?

00:14:33.321 --> 00:14:37.087
You know, I think he had
a ring on one of his hands

00:14:37.124 --> 00:14:40.184
when he touched
my shoulder, my neck.

00:14:42.196 --> 00:14:45.461
I wonder if I'll have
another dream tonight.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:47.968
I'd read two chapters.

00:15:13.828 --> 00:15:16.797
You probably want to be alone.

00:15:16.831 --> 00:15:18.128
I'll leave.

00:15:18.165 --> 00:15:19.462
No, Ned. It's okay.

00:15:19.500 --> 00:15:22.196
Look, I'm sorry we got off
to a bad start yesterday.

00:15:22.236 --> 00:15:24.704
I've been reading
my grandmother's journals

00:15:24.739 --> 00:15:26.866
and I know how much
you meant to her.

00:15:26.974 --> 00:15:28.874
Aye, she was a grand lady.

00:15:28.976 --> 00:15:31.501
You'll not see many
more like her.

00:15:31.546 --> 00:15:35.414
You have your grandmother's fire
that's for sure.

00:15:35.449 --> 00:15:38.885
Ned, you're welcome

00:15:38.953 --> 00:15:41.217
to stay at the house
after I've gone.

00:15:41.255 --> 00:15:43.587
I need someone
to take care of the place.

00:15:43.624 --> 00:15:45.353
That's very kind of you, lass

00:15:45.393 --> 00:15:47.361
but I'll ne'er set foot
in that house again

00:15:47.395 --> 00:15:49.556
and I recommend
that you do not either.

00:15:49.597 --> 00:15:51.292
Why?

00:15:51.332 --> 00:15:52.890
Like I tried to tell
your grandmother

00:15:52.967 --> 00:15:53.899
the house is haunted.

00:15:54.001 --> 00:15:56.492
Haunted?

00:15:56.537 --> 00:15:58.562
You believe what you want, lass.

00:15:58.606 --> 00:16:00.437
Just do not light that candle.

00:16:00.474 --> 00:16:01.406
Why not?

00:16:01.442 --> 00:16:04.002
It'll bring the ghost.
It's his home.

00:16:04.045 --> 00:16:07.105
Oh, he's out now,
wandering across the land

00:16:07.148 --> 00:16:09.378
angry,
angry at being driven out.

00:16:09.417 --> 00:16:11.851
That's why he's bringing
the storms.

00:16:11.886 --> 00:16:14.980
Ned, the weather system's
control is malfunctioning.

00:16:15.022 --> 00:16:17.354
The Enterprise
is trying to repair it.

00:16:17.391 --> 00:16:21.122
Oh, sure, but who do you think
is causing the malfunction?

00:16:21.162 --> 00:16:23.096
I think your imagination is...

00:16:23.130 --> 00:16:26.122
Think what you want,
see what you want.

00:16:26.167 --> 00:16:27.794
Just do as I say.

00:16:27.835 --> 00:16:29.826
Do not light that candle

00:16:29.870 --> 00:16:32.964
and do not go to that house,
or before you know it

00:16:33.007 --> 00:16:36.443
I'll be burying another Howard
in this cemetery.

00:17:06.507 --> 00:17:09.374
Captain, I am detecting
atmospheric turbulence

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:10.707
over the colony

00:17:10.745 --> 00:17:13.236
and large pockets
of electrical activity.

00:17:13.280 --> 00:17:14.269
On screen.

00:17:16.851 --> 00:17:19.513
It is growing in intensity, sir.

00:17:19.553 --> 00:17:21.783
That's one hell
of a thunderstorm.

00:17:21.822 --> 00:17:23.084
Bridge to Engineering.

00:17:23.124 --> 00:17:24.523
Mr. Data, we're reading

00:17:24.558 --> 00:17:27.527
an extremely large storm system
over the Caldos colony.

00:17:27.561 --> 00:17:30.325
I thought that the weather
control malfunction

00:17:30.364 --> 00:17:31.558
was not severe.

00:17:31.599 --> 00:17:33.624
It began as a minor
power fluctuation, sir

00:17:33.668 --> 00:17:36.728
but the effect has spread
throughout the control grid.

00:17:36.771 --> 00:17:38.864
It has caused
an unusual concentration

00:17:38.939 --> 00:17:41.305
of cumulonimbus activity
above the colony.

00:17:41.342 --> 00:17:43.810
Captain, I suggest
we set up a power transfer

00:17:43.844 --> 00:17:46.335
between the Enterprise
and the weather substations...

00:17:46.380 --> 00:17:48.974
try to give them enough power
to stabilize the storm.

00:17:49.016 --> 00:17:50.074
Make it so.

00:18:21.381 --> 00:18:22.973
Who's there?!

00:18:24.985 --> 00:18:26.111
Ned?!

00:18:26.152 --> 00:18:28.450
Is that you?

00:18:28.488 --> 00:18:30.479
Hello!

00:18:45.238 --> 00:18:48.230
I know somebody's here,
so I suggest you...

00:19:07.827 --> 00:19:10.455
All right, now, that's it.

00:19:10.497 --> 00:19:12.556
If you don't show yourself
right now

00:19:12.599 --> 00:19:14.226
I am calling the Enterprise

00:19:14.267 --> 00:19:16.735
and there
will be ten security guards here

00:19:16.770 --> 00:19:18.067
within 30 seconds.

00:19:18.104 --> 00:19:20.095
Beverly.

00:19:23.310 --> 00:19:26.575
Beverly,
I've come back for you.

00:19:26.613 --> 00:19:29.241
Who are you?

00:19:29.282 --> 00:19:31.250
Don't you remember?

00:19:31.284 --> 00:19:34.742
I came to you last night
while you were asleep.

00:19:34.788 --> 00:19:37.484
No, that was a dream.

00:19:37.524 --> 00:19:40.152
I'm calling the Enterprise.

00:19:48.802 --> 00:19:51.032
Now do you remember me?

00:19:51.071 --> 00:19:52.402
Yes.

00:19:52.439 --> 00:19:53.701
What's...

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:55.537
what's happening to me?

00:19:55.575 --> 00:19:58.305
Right now, I feel so strange.

00:19:58.345 --> 00:19:59.869
I love you, Beverly

00:19:59.946 --> 00:20:02.938
just as I loved Felisa
before you.

00:20:08.822 --> 00:20:10.346
Are you Ronin?

00:20:10.390 --> 00:20:11.448
Yes.

00:20:11.491 --> 00:20:14.756
You saw me at the funeral.

00:20:20.500 --> 00:20:22.627
Who are you?!

00:20:24.637 --> 00:20:26.832
I am a spirit.

00:20:26.873 --> 00:20:28.738
I don't believe in...

00:20:28.775 --> 00:20:30.299
Ghosts?

00:20:30.343 --> 00:20:33.312
Nor did I in the beginning.

00:20:33.346 --> 00:20:38.306
I was born in 1647
in Glasgow on Earth.

00:20:38.351 --> 00:20:41.320
You're telling me

00:20:41.354 --> 00:20:44.812
that you're
an 800-year-old ghost?

00:20:44.858 --> 00:20:48.055
I found a home
with Jessel Howard.

00:20:48.094 --> 00:20:52.394
She was a pretty lass
with a mane of red hair

00:20:52.432 --> 00:20:54.923
and eyes like diamonds.

00:20:55.035 --> 00:20:58.562
Oh, I loved her very much.

00:20:58.605 --> 00:21:00.163
When she died

00:21:00.206 --> 00:21:04.040
I stayed with her daughter
and her daughter

00:21:04.077 --> 00:21:10.038
and on down through the years,
generation after generation.

00:21:18.224 --> 00:21:22.126
And now you're here on Caldos,
200 light-years away?

00:21:22.162 --> 00:21:25.131
When your family moved out
into the galaxy

00:21:25.165 --> 00:21:26.792
I moved with them.

00:21:26.833 --> 00:21:29.267
I don't believe you.

00:21:29.302 --> 00:21:32.271
I believe you are
the most beautiful women

00:21:32.305 --> 00:21:34.466
I have ever known.

00:21:34.507 --> 00:21:36.441
Oh, what's...

00:21:36.476 --> 00:21:39.036
what's happening to me?

00:21:39.079 --> 00:21:41.445
We're becoming one, Beverly.

00:21:41.481 --> 00:21:44.814
We're going to be together.

00:21:44.851 --> 00:21:47.479
I don't understand.

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:50.318
Stop it!

00:21:56.262 --> 00:21:57.388
Come in.

00:21:57.430 --> 00:21:58.397
Hi, Bev.

00:21:58.431 --> 00:22:00.194
I just wanted too see
if you were going

00:22:00.233 --> 00:22:02.133
to Mok'bara class this morning.

00:22:02.168 --> 00:22:04.432
No, I think I'm going
to skip it today.

00:22:04.471 --> 00:22:05.802
I'm exhausted.

00:22:05.839 --> 00:22:09.866
Did you have
another dream last night?

00:22:09.976 --> 00:22:11.273
Not exactly.

00:22:11.311 --> 00:22:12.778
Is anything wrong?

00:22:12.812 --> 00:22:14.837
Not at all.

00:22:14.881 --> 00:22:17.748
Beverly, if I didn't know
any better

00:22:17.784 --> 00:22:20.412
I'd say you were seeing someone.

00:22:20.453 --> 00:22:22.318
Deanna...

00:22:22.355 --> 00:22:24.050
Now I know

00:22:24.090 --> 00:22:26.251
you're seeing someone.

00:22:26.292 --> 00:22:29.159
I'm not seeing anybody.

00:22:30.697 --> 00:22:33.029
I met someone, that's all.

00:22:33.066 --> 00:22:36.126
Well, you obviously have
romantic feelings for him.

00:22:36.169 --> 00:22:37.898
Beverly, when are you going

00:22:38.004 --> 00:22:40.871
to realize
that you can't fool me?

00:22:40.907 --> 00:22:42.204
Who is it?

00:22:42.242 --> 00:22:44.267
All right.

00:22:45.845 --> 00:22:47.710
I met Ronin.

00:22:47.747 --> 00:22:49.476
Ronin?

00:22:49.516 --> 00:22:52.007
Your grandmother's lover?

00:22:55.588 --> 00:22:58.921
He's unlike anyone
I've ever met before.

00:22:58.958 --> 00:23:01.518
I know this sounds crazy, but...

00:23:01.561 --> 00:23:04.758
I have never known
anyone who is so...

00:23:04.797 --> 00:23:05.821
Passionate.

00:23:05.865 --> 00:23:07.093
Exactly.

00:23:07.133 --> 00:23:10.227
I can see why Nana
fell in love with him.

00:23:12.238 --> 00:23:15.332
This sounds very strange,
doesn't it?

00:23:15.375 --> 00:23:17.775
I admit it's...

00:23:17.810 --> 00:23:20.040
unusual.

00:23:22.348 --> 00:23:24.782
I'm very happy for you.

00:23:28.855 --> 00:23:32.154
But I want you
to consider something.

00:23:32.192 --> 00:23:36.458
You and Ronin have both suffered
a tremendous loss.

00:23:36.496 --> 00:23:37.793
Very often

00:23:37.830 --> 00:23:41.163
shared traumatic
experience can create

00:23:41.201 --> 00:23:43.863
the illusion of closeness...

00:23:43.903 --> 00:23:45.894
and romance.

00:23:45.939 --> 00:23:48.373
Well, thank you for your concern

00:23:48.408 --> 00:23:51.002
but I think
I know what I'm doing.

00:23:51.044 --> 00:23:54.502
Besides, I didn't say
I was in love with him.

00:23:54.547 --> 00:23:56.014
I'm just intrigued.

00:24:03.523 --> 00:24:05.388
You know, Captain,
I moved to this colony

00:24:05.425 --> 00:24:07.256
because it was
a re-creation of Scotland

00:24:07.293 --> 00:24:10.057
but I must admit it's getting
to be a little too realistic.

00:24:15.235 --> 00:24:17.066
What the hell is going on?

00:24:17.103 --> 00:24:18.070
There appears to be

00:24:18.104 --> 00:24:20.004
a condensed suspension
of water vapor

00:24:20.039 --> 00:24:22.371
approximately
one degree Celsius.

00:24:22.408 --> 00:24:23.966
Fog.

00:24:24.010 --> 00:24:25.443
It just sort of rolled
in on us, sir.

00:24:25.478 --> 00:24:26.877
There has been a malfunction

00:24:26.913 --> 00:24:28.676
in the ship's
environmental control.

00:24:28.715 --> 00:24:31.616
We've traced the problem
to the power transfer beam.

00:24:31.651 --> 00:24:33.312
There's some sort
of feedback coming

00:24:33.353 --> 00:24:35.514
from one of the colony's
weather substations.

00:24:35.555 --> 00:24:36.749
Another power fluctuation?

00:24:36.789 --> 00:24:38.188
Captain

00:24:38.224 --> 00:24:41.455
the temperature in Ten-Forward
has dropped below freezing

00:24:41.494 --> 00:24:43.155
and deck 13 has lost gravity.

00:24:43.196 --> 00:24:45.892
Mr. Data, disengage
the power transfer.

00:24:45.965 --> 00:24:48.900
I am unable to terminate
the connection, sir.

00:24:48.968 --> 00:24:52.028
A feedback loop has formed
in the transfer beam.

00:24:52.071 --> 00:24:54.301
I will have to go
to the substation

00:24:54.340 --> 00:24:57.275
and attempt to correct
the problem from there.

00:24:57.310 --> 00:24:58.607
Make it so.

00:24:58.645 --> 00:25:02.274
In the meantime,
I think I'll go get my jacket.

00:25:07.753 --> 00:25:09.846
I have analyzed
the control module

00:25:09.922 --> 00:25:11.947
in the primary
weather control grid.

00:25:11.991 --> 00:25:13.390
It appears the station

00:25:13.425 --> 00:25:15.859
is experiencing a
system-wide power failure.

00:25:15.961 --> 00:25:16.950
This is impossible.

00:25:16.996 --> 00:25:18.691
The backup system
should have...

00:25:19.765 --> 00:25:21.232
Excuse me, sir.

00:25:21.266 --> 00:25:22.631
You are dismantling

00:25:22.668 --> 00:25:25.102
the primary power conduit.

00:25:25.137 --> 00:25:26.104
I must ask you to stop.

00:25:26.138 --> 00:25:27.127
No!

00:25:30.809 --> 00:25:32.174
Get away from me!

00:25:33.545 --> 00:25:34.603
You don't understand!

00:25:34.647 --> 00:25:37.013
He's trying to kill us all!

00:25:48.827 --> 00:25:50.419
He is dead.

00:25:57.002 --> 00:25:59.266
From what I can tell,
he was trying to shut down

00:25:59.304 --> 00:26:00.771
the entire
weather control system.

00:26:00.806 --> 00:26:02.774
He was pulling out
the primary plasma conduit.

00:26:02.808 --> 00:26:03.934
It's probably what caused

00:26:03.976 --> 00:26:05.603
the plasma discharge
that killed him.

00:26:05.644 --> 00:26:06.668
I knew Ned Quint.

00:26:06.712 --> 00:26:07.838
He was an honest man.

00:26:07.880 --> 00:26:09.279
He kept mostly to himself.

00:26:09.314 --> 00:26:11.782
I don't know why he'd
try something like that.

00:26:11.817 --> 00:26:13.717
Well, it's going
to take us some time

00:26:13.752 --> 00:26:15.344
to get the system back on line.

00:26:15.387 --> 00:26:17.321
I'd say we need
another day at least.

00:26:17.356 --> 00:26:19.119
In the meantime, Governor
you should expect

00:26:19.158 --> 00:26:20.523
the weather problems
to continue.

00:26:20.559 --> 00:26:23.392
I think you better
take a look at this.

00:26:26.565 --> 00:26:29.432
Data, you said
there was a plasma discharge

00:26:29.468 --> 00:26:32.062
from the console
when Quint was killed.

00:26:32.104 --> 00:26:33.128
That is correct.

00:26:33.172 --> 00:26:34.867
Well, that wasn't
what killed him.

00:26:34.973 --> 00:26:36.338
I'm detecting an anomalous

00:26:36.375 --> 00:26:38.275
energy residual
throughout his body

00:26:38.310 --> 00:26:40.141
right down
to the cellular level.

00:26:40.179 --> 00:26:41.373
Whatever it is

00:26:41.413 --> 00:26:45.144
it wasn't the result
of a plasma discharge.

00:26:45.184 --> 00:26:47.618
Anything?

00:26:47.653 --> 00:26:49.712
I cannot identify
the energy residual.

00:26:49.755 --> 00:26:52.849
However, it appears to have
the same anaphasic signature

00:26:52.891 --> 00:26:54.290
as the power fluctuations

00:26:54.326 --> 00:26:56.760
we observed from
the weather control system.

00:26:56.795 --> 00:26:57.887
It's possible
that whatever caused

00:26:57.996 --> 00:26:59.554
the weather malfunctions
also killed Quint.

00:26:59.598 --> 00:27:01.623
It is possible.

00:27:01.667 --> 00:27:04.602
We should scan the colony
for any energy readings

00:27:04.636 --> 00:27:06.797
that match
this anaphasic signature.

00:27:08.307 --> 00:27:10.172
Governor, with your permission

00:27:10.209 --> 00:27:12.837
I'd like to take the body
back to the ship

00:27:12.911 --> 00:27:14.276
to run further tests.

00:27:14.313 --> 00:27:15.473
Of course, Doctor.

00:27:15.514 --> 00:27:18.347
Ensign, ask Dr. Selar
to run a biospectral analysis.

00:27:18.383 --> 00:27:19.543
Yes, Doctor.

00:27:19.585 --> 00:27:21.849
You're not going to run
the tests yourself?

00:27:21.887 --> 00:27:24.219
No, I have some things
I need to attend to.

00:27:31.930 --> 00:27:34.660
Ronin, I've got to talk to you.

00:27:34.700 --> 00:27:35.860
Are you here?

00:27:35.901 --> 00:27:37.163
I'm here.

00:27:37.202 --> 00:27:41.036
Beverly, did you miss me?

00:27:41.073 --> 00:27:43.007
Yes.

00:27:43.041 --> 00:27:46.238
But I must talk to you.

00:27:46.278 --> 00:27:48.246
There's been an accident.

00:27:48.280 --> 00:27:49.611
I know.

00:27:49.648 --> 00:27:51.377
Quint is dead.

00:27:51.416 --> 00:27:53.281
Well, why did it happen?

00:27:53.318 --> 00:27:54.751
What was he doing?

00:27:54.787 --> 00:27:58.120
Beverly, there's
something more important

00:27:58.157 --> 00:27:59.886
we should talk about.

00:27:59.958 --> 00:28:01.789
Ronin, I've got to know.

00:28:01.827 --> 00:28:03.522
Quint's dead.

00:28:06.865 --> 00:28:08.025
Ronin.

00:28:08.066 --> 00:28:09.658
Yes.

00:28:12.037 --> 00:28:13.698
I need you to help me.

00:28:13.739 --> 00:28:15.036
Help you?

00:28:15.073 --> 00:28:19.806
It's not easy for me
to take corporeal form.

00:28:19.845 --> 00:28:22.370
I can't do it for long.

00:28:25.684 --> 00:28:28.118
I want you to light the candle.

00:28:28.153 --> 00:28:30.849
Quint said you lived
in the candle.

00:28:30.956 --> 00:28:32.014
Is that true?

00:28:32.057 --> 00:28:35.288
Yes, if I'm away
from it for too long

00:28:35.327 --> 00:28:36.954
I begin to weaken.

00:28:36.995 --> 00:28:40.055
That's why the women
in your family

00:28:40.098 --> 00:28:42.999
have always kept the candle lit.

00:28:43.035 --> 00:28:45.265
The candle's on the ship.

00:28:45.304 --> 00:28:46.669
I'll go get it.

00:28:46.705 --> 00:28:48.229
No.

00:28:48.273 --> 00:28:51.037
I must go with you.

00:28:51.076 --> 00:28:52.475
How?

00:28:52.511 --> 00:28:55.708
The power transfer beam...
I can travel along it.

00:28:55.747 --> 00:28:58.477
Then when the candle's lit,
then what happens?

00:28:58.517 --> 00:29:00.985
Then we'll be together...

00:29:01.019 --> 00:29:03.385
always.

00:29:44.162 --> 00:29:46.392
Computer, secure door.

00:30:10.255 --> 00:30:11.688
I lit the candle.

00:30:11.723 --> 00:30:12.985
Where are you?

00:30:22.834 --> 00:30:26.031
Shh, shh.
It's all right.

00:30:26.071 --> 00:30:27.436
We're together.

00:30:27.472 --> 00:30:30.168
We're going to be one.

00:30:30.208 --> 00:30:32.108
I'm going to become
part of you, Beverly.

00:30:32.144 --> 00:30:34.009
Would you like that?

00:30:34.046 --> 00:30:35.741
Oh, yes, more than anything.

00:30:35.781 --> 00:30:38.375
As it was with your grandmother
and your great-grandmother

00:30:38.417 --> 00:30:40.715
and all of the Howard women
before them.

00:30:40.752 --> 00:30:43.585
I'll take care of you

00:30:43.622 --> 00:30:51.188
and you will feel love
as you've never felt it before.

00:31:19.658 --> 00:31:21.455
Beverly, what the hell is this?

00:31:21.493 --> 00:31:23.893
I thought it was
pretty self-explanatory.

00:31:23.962 --> 00:31:25.293
I'm leaving Starfleet.

00:31:25.330 --> 00:31:26.558
Energize.

00:31:26.598 --> 00:31:27.724
Belay that order.

00:31:27.766 --> 00:31:29.358
Aye, sir.

00:31:29.401 --> 00:31:32.529
Beverly, you can't just resign.

00:31:32.571 --> 00:31:34.300
I can, and I have.

00:31:34.339 --> 00:31:36.068
I've decided to stay on Caldos

00:31:36.108 --> 00:31:38.372
and become a healer
like my grandmother.

00:31:38.410 --> 00:31:40.901
It's a proud Howard tradition

00:31:41.013 --> 00:31:43.447
and I've decided to uphold it.
Energize.

00:31:48.020 --> 00:31:49.920
I've resigned my commission

00:31:50.022 --> 00:31:52.820
so, unless you plan
on kidnapping me...

00:32:10.440 --> 00:32:12.408
Beverly was attracted to Ronin

00:32:12.442 --> 00:32:17.072
in a very intense
and... intimate way.

00:32:17.114 --> 00:32:21.050
I warned her that it
was all very sudden

00:32:21.084 --> 00:32:23.177
but she didn't want
to talk about it

00:32:23.220 --> 00:32:24.346
so I let her alone.

00:32:24.388 --> 00:32:26.322
I sensed that she was
holding something back.

00:32:26.356 --> 00:32:28.221
That she wasn't telling me
the whole truth.

00:32:28.258 --> 00:32:30.021
Do you think this Ronin could be

00:32:30.060 --> 00:32:32.756
exerting some sort
of influence over her?

00:32:32.796 --> 00:32:35.697
That it's because of him
that she's staying?

00:32:35.732 --> 00:32:37.256
It's possible

00:32:37.301 --> 00:32:40.134
but she may really believe
she's in love with him.

00:32:40.170 --> 00:32:42.900
This is a rash decision.

00:32:43.006 --> 00:32:44.200
Ill-considered.

00:32:44.241 --> 00:32:45.572
It's not like Beverly at all.

00:32:45.609 --> 00:32:46.837
I agree

00:32:46.877 --> 00:32:49.903
but she does have the right
to make that choice

00:32:50.013 --> 00:32:52.573
even if we don't feel
it's a good one.

00:32:55.285 --> 00:32:56.718
Come.

00:32:56.753 --> 00:33:01.452
Captain, Geordi and I have
detected an energy residual

00:33:01.491 --> 00:33:03.721
with the same
anaphasic signature

00:33:03.760 --> 00:33:06.058
as the one we found
on Ned Quint's body.

00:33:06.096 --> 00:33:07.961
Where?

00:33:07.998 --> 00:33:10.796
Approximately 17 kilometers from
the center of the colony, sir.

00:33:10.834 --> 00:33:12.233
It is coming from the cemetery.

00:33:14.271 --> 00:33:17.968
Data, I want you to go
down to the cemetery.

00:33:18.008 --> 00:33:19.703
See if you can
pinpoint the source.

00:33:19.743 --> 00:33:21.370
Aye, sir.

00:33:22.612 --> 00:33:23.806
In the meantime

00:33:23.847 --> 00:33:29.513
I would like to meet
with this Ronin.

00:33:38.328 --> 00:33:41.456
The energy readings are coming
from this direction

00:33:41.498 --> 00:33:44.467
but I can't get
an exact location.

00:33:44.501 --> 00:33:47.061
I'll try narrowing
the scan field.

00:33:47.104 --> 00:33:49.868
The energy readings
appear to be originating

00:33:49.906 --> 00:33:52.374
approximately two meters
below the surface.

00:33:58.682 --> 00:34:03.085
I believe they are concentrated
within this burial site.

00:34:17.234 --> 00:34:20.567
I'm so glad you're here.

00:34:20.604 --> 00:34:22.834
I can't imagine

00:34:22.873 --> 00:34:25.865
what life was like
before I met you.

00:34:25.909 --> 00:34:29.003
And it will only get better.

00:34:41.425 --> 00:34:44.189
Oh, Ronin.

00:34:44.227 --> 00:34:48.027
I had no idea
I could feel this way.

00:34:48.065 --> 00:34:50.295
We're nearly merged now

00:34:50.333 --> 00:34:52.858
as two candles join
to form a single light

00:34:52.903 --> 00:34:55.463
so we will flourish as one.

00:34:57.074 --> 00:35:01.170
I love you, Beverly.

00:35:03.480 --> 00:35:06.415
I love you.

00:35:21.598 --> 00:35:23.031
Beverly?

00:35:25.135 --> 00:35:26.363
Jean-Luc.

00:35:26.403 --> 00:35:28.371
I'm sorry I startled you.

00:35:28.405 --> 00:35:31.169
I knocked,
but there was no answer.

00:35:31.208 --> 00:35:32.266
The door was open.

00:35:32.309 --> 00:35:33.606
I hope you don't mind.

00:35:33.643 --> 00:35:35.042
What do you want?

00:35:35.078 --> 00:35:38.241
Well, I'd hoped to meet
your new friend Ronin.

00:35:38.281 --> 00:35:39.305
He's not here.

00:35:39.349 --> 00:35:41.249
Well, perhaps I could wait

00:35:41.284 --> 00:35:42.615
if you don't mind.

00:35:42.652 --> 00:35:45.780
I'm really anxious to meet
this remarkable young man

00:35:45.822 --> 00:35:49.724
who has swept away not just one,
but two of the Howard women.

00:35:51.094 --> 00:35:53.790
Jealousy doesn't suit you,
Jean-Luc.

00:35:53.830 --> 00:35:55.491
Have you...

00:35:55.532 --> 00:35:57.830
have you changed
the color of your eyes?

00:35:57.868 --> 00:36:01.269
I... I just grew tired
of the other color.

00:36:01.304 --> 00:36:03.534
Don't you think it suits me?

00:36:03.573 --> 00:36:05.541
I think that I preferred

00:36:05.575 --> 00:36:08.476
your eyes the way
they were before.

00:36:08.512 --> 00:36:12.107
I think I preferred you the way
you were before, Beverly.

00:36:12.149 --> 00:36:14.845
Well, this is the way I am now

00:36:14.918 --> 00:36:16.852
and this is my life.

00:36:16.920 --> 00:36:18.444
I've made my decision

00:36:18.488 --> 00:36:20.820
and I'm not going
to change my mind

00:36:20.857 --> 00:36:22.848
so please leave me alone.

00:36:22.893 --> 00:36:24.326
Oh, no,
there's something's wrong.

00:36:24.361 --> 00:36:25.851
Now, Beverly,
this is more than just

00:36:25.962 --> 00:36:29.090
an obsessive love affair
that has got out of hand.

00:36:29.132 --> 00:36:30.861
Tell me, why is it that no one

00:36:30.934 --> 00:36:32.834
has seen this Ronin except you?

00:36:34.004 --> 00:36:36.632
All right, Captain.

00:36:36.673 --> 00:36:38.436
Here I am.

00:36:45.081 --> 00:36:48.414
I believe Beverly asked you
to leave her alone.

00:36:50.153 --> 00:36:51.814
So, you're Ronin.

00:36:51.855 --> 00:36:54.119
It's a pleasure to meet you.

00:36:54.157 --> 00:36:55.317
Where are you from?

00:36:55.358 --> 00:36:57.326
Earth. Scotland.

00:36:57.360 --> 00:37:01.023
How long have you been
on Caldos?

00:37:01.064 --> 00:37:03.396
All that matters
is that I'm here now

00:37:03.433 --> 00:37:06.129
and that Beverly and I
plan to be together

00:37:06.169 --> 00:37:07.830
for the rest of our lives.

00:37:07.904 --> 00:37:09.030
Data to Picard.

00:37:09.072 --> 00:37:10.039
Go ahead, Data.

00:37:10.073 --> 00:37:11.631
Captain,
we have located the source

00:37:11.675 --> 00:37:13.074
of the energy residual.

00:37:13.109 --> 00:37:15.373
It appears to be concentrated

00:37:15.412 --> 00:37:17.277
within Felisa Howard's coffin.

00:37:17.314 --> 00:37:20.147
Captain, we'd like permission
to exhume the body.

00:37:20.183 --> 00:37:22.481
You can't do that.

00:37:22.519 --> 00:37:24.453
Leave her alone.

00:37:24.487 --> 00:37:25.454
Why not?

00:37:25.488 --> 00:37:26.853
What are you afraid of?

00:37:26.923 --> 00:37:28.447
I'm not afraid of anything

00:37:28.491 --> 00:37:32.757
but I cannot allow you
to desecrate her grave.

00:37:32.796 --> 00:37:35.264
Data, ask Governor Maturin's
permission

00:37:35.298 --> 00:37:36.595
to exhume the body.

00:37:36.633 --> 00:37:38.066
Picard out.

00:37:38.101 --> 00:37:40.092
I won't stand for this.

00:37:40.136 --> 00:37:42.536
I'll go to the Governor myself.

00:37:42.572 --> 00:37:43.971
Go on.

00:37:44.007 --> 00:37:46.874
I wouldn't be surprised
if he doesn't know who you are.

00:37:46.977 --> 00:37:49.036
He'll probably have
the same questions

00:37:49.079 --> 00:37:50.046
that I do.

00:37:50.080 --> 00:37:51.513
How did you get here?

00:37:51.548 --> 00:37:52.674
What ship did you come on?

00:37:52.716 --> 00:37:53.876
Jean-Luc, leave him alone.

00:37:53.984 --> 00:37:55.781
Why don't you answer
my questions? What ship?

00:37:55.819 --> 00:37:58.652
I'd like to take a look
at the passenger list.

00:37:58.688 --> 00:38:00.087
Where have you been living here?

00:38:00.123 --> 00:38:01.181
What's your position?

00:38:01.224 --> 00:38:02.452
Who are your neighbors?

00:38:06.062 --> 00:38:07.029
Come on, Beverly.

00:38:07.063 --> 00:38:08.690
We've got to get out of here.

00:38:10.100 --> 00:38:12.091
Jean-Luc!

00:38:20.410 --> 00:38:22.139
Beverly, we must
stop the others.

00:38:22.178 --> 00:38:23.406
They cannot exhume the body.

00:38:23.446 --> 00:38:24.572
We can't just leave him.

00:38:24.614 --> 00:38:25.581
He might die.

00:38:25.615 --> 00:38:26.809
You must come.

00:38:26.850 --> 00:38:27.976
I am your love.

00:38:28.018 --> 00:38:30.248
I am the one
who will take care of you.

00:38:30.287 --> 00:38:33.381
I can't just let him die.

00:38:33.423 --> 00:38:35.857
Beverly, come with me!

00:38:35.892 --> 00:38:38.258
No.

00:38:38.295 --> 00:38:39.626
No!

00:38:42.966 --> 00:38:45.127
I'm sorry.

00:38:45.168 --> 00:38:47.159
I'm going to stop them.

00:38:58.181 --> 00:39:01.378
Come on, come on.

00:39:06.256 --> 00:39:07.553
I'm all right.

00:39:07.590 --> 00:39:09.148
Beverly, go after him.

00:39:09.192 --> 00:39:10.921
Go to the cemetery.

00:39:15.632 --> 00:39:18.032
La Forge to Enterprise.
We're ready down here.

00:39:18.068 --> 00:39:19.330
Aye, sir.

00:39:37.287 --> 00:39:39.346
I am reading definite signs

00:39:39.389 --> 00:39:41.823
of anaphasic energy
in her body.

00:39:41.858 --> 00:39:44.088
It appears to extend
to the cellular level.

00:39:44.127 --> 00:39:45.253
That's impossible.

00:39:45.295 --> 00:39:47.525
She was nowhere near
the weather station

00:39:47.564 --> 00:39:48.861
when Quint was killed.

00:39:48.898 --> 00:39:50.195
She died of natural causes.

00:39:50.233 --> 00:39:52.064
I suggest we run
a deep tissue scan

00:39:52.102 --> 00:39:53.660
to look for any signs of...

00:39:58.708 --> 00:40:00.073
No!

00:40:00.110 --> 00:40:03.273
Ronin, stop this.

00:40:03.313 --> 00:40:04.837
Stop this, please.

00:40:04.881 --> 00:40:07.281
Beverly, it's all right.

00:40:07.317 --> 00:40:08.875
Have trust in me.

00:40:08.918 --> 00:40:10.078
You're not Nana.

00:40:10.120 --> 00:40:12.611
Nana's dead.

00:40:12.655 --> 00:40:14.456
Leave her alone!

00:40:17.325 --> 00:40:20.089
Beverly!

00:40:20.128 --> 00:40:21.288
Forgive me.

00:40:21.329 --> 00:40:23.388
These men were trying
to stop us

00:40:23.431 --> 00:40:24.796
from being together.

00:40:24.833 --> 00:40:25.891
Once they're gone

00:40:26.000 --> 00:40:27.297
everything will be right.

00:40:27.335 --> 00:40:28.302
No, it won't.

00:40:28.336 --> 00:40:29.633
You've been infusing me

00:40:29.671 --> 00:40:31.298
with the same sort
of anaphasic energy

00:40:31.339 --> 00:40:32.363
that killed Quint.

00:40:32.407 --> 00:40:34.807
He was trying to destroy me.

00:40:34.843 --> 00:40:38.904
I had to defend myself.

00:40:39.013 --> 00:40:41.811
Oh, my love.

00:40:41.850 --> 00:40:44.910
I would never harm you.

00:40:45.019 --> 00:40:47.317
I am here to protect you.

00:40:47.355 --> 00:40:49.823
No, you're not.

00:40:49.858 --> 00:40:52.656
There's no such thing
as a ghost.

00:40:52.694 --> 00:40:56.926
You are some sort
of anaphasic life-form.

00:40:56.998 --> 00:40:59.193
Anaphasic energy
is extremely unstable.

00:40:59.234 --> 00:41:00.633
It needs an organic host

00:41:00.668 --> 00:41:02.863
in order to maintain
molecular cohesion

00:41:02.904 --> 00:41:05.031
or else you'll die,
isn't that right?

00:41:05.073 --> 00:41:06.040
Beverly.

00:41:06.074 --> 00:41:07.336
I also scanned the candle.

00:41:07.375 --> 00:41:08.865
The flame is plasma-based.

00:41:08.910 --> 00:41:11.208
You were using it
as a receptacle for yourself

00:41:11.246 --> 00:41:13.214
in order to get to me.

00:41:13.248 --> 00:41:14.977
In order to merge with me!

00:41:15.016 --> 00:41:18.110
You have been using me,
Nana, my entire family

00:41:18.152 --> 00:41:19.278
for centuries!

00:41:19.320 --> 00:41:21.880
And I loved all of them!

00:41:21.990 --> 00:41:24.083
And they loved me.

00:41:29.330 --> 00:41:31.855
Give me the candle, Beverly.

00:41:31.900 --> 00:41:35.392
No, no.

00:41:41.609 --> 00:41:43.907
Put it down...

00:41:44.012 --> 00:41:45.980
or I will kill him.

00:41:49.484 --> 00:41:52.510
Set it down and walk away.

00:42:02.130 --> 00:42:03.893
No!

00:42:06.134 --> 00:42:07.567
Crusher to Riker.

00:42:07.602 --> 00:42:09.399
Will, close off
all the plasma conduits

00:42:09.437 --> 00:42:11.200
in the weather control systems.

00:42:11.239 --> 00:42:12.365
I'll explain later.

00:42:12.407 --> 00:42:14.307
Understood.

00:42:17.645 --> 00:42:19.875
You've nowhere left to go.

00:42:23.651 --> 00:42:27.485
Yes... I do.

00:42:31.593 --> 00:42:32.924
Keep away from me.

00:42:41.336 --> 00:42:44.464
Beverly.

00:42:44.505 --> 00:42:46.268
I love you.

00:42:47.675 --> 00:42:48.972
Bever...

00:43:00.388 --> 00:43:02.583
Captain's Log, supplemental.

00:43:02.624 --> 00:43:05.593
Commander La Forge and Mr. Data
have recovered

00:43:05.627 --> 00:43:08.858
from their exposure
to the anaphasic energy

00:43:08.963 --> 00:43:11.431
but I'm afraid
Dr. Crusher's recovery

00:43:11.466 --> 00:43:13.798
will be
of a more personal nature.

00:43:13.835 --> 00:43:17.498
Somehow, he realized
that one of my ancestors

00:43:17.538 --> 00:43:19.028
had a biochemistry

00:43:19.073 --> 00:43:22.634
that was compatible
with his energy matrix.

00:43:26.814 --> 00:43:29.806
I imagine that he
took on human form

00:43:29.851 --> 00:43:32.411
and seduced her like he did me.

00:43:34.489 --> 00:43:37.185
I was about to be initiated

00:43:37.225 --> 00:43:40.456
into a very unusual
relationship.

00:43:40.495 --> 00:43:43.430
You might call it
a family tradition.

00:43:43.464 --> 00:43:47.127
But there's a part of me
that's a little sad.

00:43:47.168 --> 00:43:48.533
How so?

00:43:48.569 --> 00:43:56.340
I re-read the entries
in my grandmother's journals.

00:43:56.377 --> 00:43:58.902
Whatever else he might
have done

00:43:59.013 --> 00:44:01.573
he made her very happy.
